# Machine-specific generated artifacts — NOT committed (Time Machine covers backup).
# CATALOG.md is rendered from registry/catalog-notes.toml ⋈ this device's live
# `three_eyes observe`, so it differs per machine. Regenerate: python -m three_eyes catalog --write
CATALOG.md

# Belt-and-suspenders (also ignored in config/.gitignore): the activation config.
config/runtime.env

# Machine-local registry overlay — jobs/commands with absolute, machine-specific
# paths (e.g. adopted cross-repo automations). Runtime reads them; the committed
# DASHBOARD.md excludes them so it stays fleet-portable. The .example + README are
# committed to document the mechanism; the real overlay files are per-machine.
registry/jobs.local.d/*.toml
registry/commands.local.allow
